-- title:
--   Norm-conjugator carries M₂(Kᵥ) into the twisted commutant
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L$ a $K$-algebra of degree $2$, let $\sigma$ be a $K$-algebra automorphism of $L$ such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in the subgroup generated by $\sigma$, and let $\delta_0 \in GL_2(L)$, $c$ a unit of $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ and $u$ an idelic unit of $K$. Write $\delta = (\delta_0 \otimes 1)\cdot \mathrm{scalar}(c) \in GL_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, where $\delta_0 \otimes 1$ is the image of $\delta_0$ under entrywise `Algebra.TensorProduct.includeLeftRingHom`. Assume: (hN) the norm string of $\delta$, that is the ordered product $\prod_{i<2}\sigma^i(\delta)$ of the iterates of $\delta$ under the automorphism of $GL_2(L\otimes_K\mathbb{A}_K)$ induced by $\sigma$, equals the image of the central scalar matrix $\mathrm{diag}(u,u)$ under $g \mapsto 1 \otimes g$; (hns) for all $x \in GL_2(L)$ and $z \in L^\times$ one has $x^{-1}\delta_0\,\sigma(x) \neq \mathrm{scalar}(z)$. Fix a finite place $v$ of $K$ (a height-one prime of $\mathcal{O}_K$) and let $\delta_v \in GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ be the image of $\delta$ under the place map [`AutomorphicForm.tensorPlace`](def/AutomorphicForm_BaseChangePlaces.html#L49). Let $\tau$ be a Haar measure on the $\sigma$-twisted centraliser `twistedCentralizer` of $\delta_v$ in $GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, let $t_v \in [0,\infty]$, and let $y \in GL_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ satisfy: (hy) $y$ is a norm conjugator for $\delta_v$ and the element $\gamma_v \in GL_2(K_v)$ obtained from $\mathrm{diag}(u,u)$ by passing to the finite adeles and then to the component at $v$, that is $1 \otimes \gamma_v = y^{-1}\cdot(\text{norm string of }\delta_v)\cdot y$; and (hmap) the pushforward of $\tau$ along $t \mapsto y^{-1}ty$ equals $t_v$ times the pushforward of the Haar measure [`AutomorphicForm.localHaar`](def/AutomorphicForm_LocalOrbitalBase.html#L168) on $GL_2(K_v)$ along $g \mapsto 1 \otimes g$, the groups being given their Borel structures. Then for every matrix $g \in M_2(K_v)$ the conjugate $y\,(1\otimes g)\,y^{-1}$ lies in the twisted commutant of $\delta_0 \otimes 1 \in GL_2(L\otimes_K K_v)$, namely in the $K$-subalgebra of $X \in M_2(L \otimes_K K_v)$ with $X\,(\delta_0 \otimes 1) = (\delta_0 \otimes 1)\,X^{\sigma}$, where $X^\sigma$ is the entrywise application of $\sigma \otimes \mathrm{id}$.
--
--   This is the local step identifying the conjugate $y^{-1}T'_v y$ of the twisted centraliser at $v$ with $1 \otimes GL_2(K_v)$ through the supports of the two Haar measures in (hmap), and deducing that conjugation by $y$ sends the whole matrix algebra $M_2(K_v)$ into the twisted commutant of $\delta_0 \otimes 1$, an order-theoretic embedding of the kind used in quaternionic twisted orbital integrals. It is used by [`AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_map_conj_eq_smul_map_toTensorGL_localHaar`](thm.html#AutomorphicForm.setLIntegral_lattice_norm_det_mul_norm_four_eq_mul_sqrt_norm_det_trace_of_map_conj_eq_smul_map_toTensorGL_localHaar) in the computation of local covolumes.
